[Music]  welcome to your weekly ticket  a willy wonka prequel is in the works  warner brothers is preparing for a third  movie which will be helmed by paddington  director paul king  this time around the film will be a  prequel called wonka which will  dive deeper into the backstory of how  young willy wonka became a candy company  and how he met the oompa loompas  which we did learn a little bit about  through johnny depp's charlie and the  chocolate factory  as for who will play wonka this time  around early casting rumors suggest  timothy chalamet  and tom holland are among those  potentially being eyed for the role  let them fight after a nearly year-long  delay due to the ongoing covet 19  pandemic  godzilla vs kong is finally here  but the fourth monsterverse movie  definitely packs a punch with tons of  monster action for fans to look forward  to  the film is directed by adam wingard  with a script from pirates of the  caribbean writer terry rozio  in addition to the titular behemoths it  stars alexander skarsgard  millie bobby brown rebecca hall and  brian tyree henry  you'll finally be able to see the film  in theaters on march 26th  and searchlight pictures has updated its  2021 release  calendar which includes guillermo del  toro's nightmare alley which is now set  for release on december 3rd  this is the first film that del toro has  directed since winning best director and  best picture at the 2017 oscars for  the shape of water nightmare alley is  based off the 1946 novel of the same  name by william lindsey gresham which is  a carnival set mystery  involving a famous mind reading act this  new adaptation has an a-list cast which  includes bradley cooper  cate blanchett rooney mara willem dafoe  richard jenkins  and tony collette to name a few  today we're celebrating the release of  the little things being available to  watch in theaters on friday by  talking to the film's cast denzel  washington jared leto and rami malek  take a look at what they had to say to  fandango correspondent nikki novak  about how a surprising amount of improv  went into shaping their roles  you wouldn't think that a movie like  this would have a lot of improv and yet  that we've heard that it did  even including jared you singing  somewhere over the rainbow at one point  to denzel's character  so i wanted to ask first i'll ask denzel  how does  improv inform how did it inform your  performance in this movie and are you a  fan of improv  i never really improvised before i work  with spike or not to that degree  as i did on mobetta blues there's a  place for it sometimes  and you and you try it it may work it  may not work but uh  i'm all for it if it fits what did you  learn about your character when you were  improvising i know you really got to go  over the top and learn things but how  did it inform your performance  well i think humor is always a great  place to  you know uh experiment with improv  because  you know i always think about jokes or  like it's like an open avocado it only  lasts for so long before it gets brown  you know it's you know so surprise is  good with humor  and um so i found that pretty useful  uh because it suited the character like  denzel said if it  if it's appropriate then then it's great  it uh you can also  you know ruin a scene uh if it goes off  the rails too much but  i'm quite a big fan of it when when the  opportunity arises  so what was the moment that it went off  the rails was it the somewhere over the  rainbow or was there something even  wilder that maybe ended up even on the  cutting edge i don't know maybe it was  when i talked about potato skins i'm not  sure  really did that actually mommy yeah  ronnie  there  did that happen and rami what did you  learn about i know you've obviously  watched  these two actors perform before but  performing opposite them  in those moments in those improv moments  and even in the scripted moments what  did you learn about your cast mates as  performers well it's it's exactly what  you're talking about in reference to  improv it may not uh always be literal  but  every time you stepped in a scene you  just don't know what's going to happen  and i think that's such a great form of  improvisation  and you know you only get that with some  of the finest actors so  that's what i experienced what was the  moment that surprised you  every moment you work with these two  guys is going to be  surprising i i don't think i could walk  in on set  and tell you what denzel or what jared  was gonna do in any given moment  and i think that's really evident in the  film and i think that's evident when i  watched it i had no idea where it was  going  and you don't want to blame because you  don't want to miss anything so thank the  three of you i get a lot of award  screeners and this is among my favorites  so thank you all very much  thank you so much  also available to watch in theaters on  friday is saint maude  i have a responsibility oh yes of course  this is life and death on another level  mod played by morphed clark is a newly  devout hospice nurse who becomes  obsessed with saving her dying patient's  soul  but sinister forces and her own sinful  past threatened to put an  end to her holy calling the film which  marks the feature film debut for writer  director rose glass is currently  certified fresh with a 97 on the tomato  meter  [Music]  and available to watch at home on friday  is savage  hey none of us are angels probably the  opposite  we wouldn't be gangsters if we always  did what we were told  why do you wear that mask  so you can see who i am  inspired by the true stories of new  zealand's street gangs across 30 years  savage follows dany at three defining  moments in his life  from the abusive state-run boys  institutions of the 60s  to the emerging urban gang scene in the  70s where disenfranchised teenagers  created their own families on the  streets  to the 80s when gangs became more  structured and violent  together the three chapters of dany's  life combined to create a deeper look at  a boy  who grows up to become the brutal  enforcer of a gang  alright well that's it for today but  leave us a comment and let us know what  you'll be watching this week  i'm kale and i'll see you next time  [Music]

